<h1>Croatian Inflectional  Grammar</h1>Version of September 11, 2026, 1:02 pm<br />Documentation available at <a href="http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar" target="_blank">http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar</a><br />Tagset available at <a href="../dictionary/export_tagset.php" target="_blank">Export UNDL Foundation tagset</a>.<br /><br /><b>M0</b><br />Invariant<br /><br /><b>M1</b><br />Irregular: rules are defined inside the entry in the dictionary<br /><br /><b>M2</b><br />Inanimate masculine nouns whose stems do not end in a palatal consonant. (<i>parobrod, alat, predmet</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M3</b><br />Animate masculine nouns whose stems do not end in a palatal consonant. (<i>kandidat, leptir, advokat, susjed</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M4</b><br />Animate masculine nouns whose stems end in a palatal consonant (č, ć, dž, đ, j, lj, nj, š and ž). (<i>kovač, pjevač, muž</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"em";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M5</b><br />Inanimate masculine nouns whose stems end in a palatal consonant (č, ć, dž, đ, j, lj, nj, š and ž). (<i>usisavač, žarač, odvijač</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"em";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M6</b><br />Animate masculine nouns whose base form ends in "k". "K" is replaced by "č" in singular vocative, and by "c" in all plural forms except for genitive and accusative. (<i>učenik, ujak, nećak, manijak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"č",0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"c",0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"c",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"c",0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"c",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"c",0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M7</b><br />Animate masculine nouns whose base form ends in "g". "G" is replaced by "ž" in singular vocative, and by "z" all plural forms except for genitive and accusative. (<i>biolog, onkolog</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"ž",0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"z",0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"z",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"z",0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"z",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"z",0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M8</b><br />Animate masculine nouns whose base form ends in "h" - "h" is replaced by "š" to form singular vocative, and by "s" to form all plural cases except for genitive and accusative. (<i>zloduh, duh, eunuh, pastuh</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"š",0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"s",0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"s",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"s",0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"s",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"s",0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M9</b><br />Animate masculine nouns whose base form ends in "c". "C" is replaced by "č" in singular vocative and in all plural cases. (<i>stric</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"č",0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"em";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"č",0>"evi";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"č",0>"eva";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"č",0>"evima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"č",0>"eve";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"č",0>"evi";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"č",0>"evima";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"č",0>"evima";<br /><br /><b>M10</b><br />Animate masculine nouns whose base form ends in "bak". "b" is replaced by "p", "a" is deleted, and appropriate case endings are added. This goes for all cases except for plural genitive. "k" is replaced by "č" in singular vocative, and by "c" in all plural cases except for genitive and accusative. (<i>golubak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"p",0>"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"p",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC:=3>"p",0>"ka";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"p",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"p",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"p",0>"kom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"p",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"p",0>"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"p",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M11</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in "lac" (except for nouns such as ilegalac, provincijalac, bijelac, etc. - these nouns are inflected according to a different paradigm). "l" is replaced by "o" in all singular cases except for nominative, and in all plural cases except for genitive.  (<i>spasilac, mislilac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"o",0>"ca";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"o",0>"cu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=3>"o",0>"ca";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"o",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"o",0>"cu";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"o",0>"cem";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"o",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"o",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"o",0>"ce";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"o",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"o",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"o",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M12</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in "dac" or "tac". (<i>sudac, otac, svetac, domorodac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"c",0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"c",0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=3>"c",0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"č",0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"c",0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"c",0>"em";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"c",0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"c",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"c",0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"c",0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"c",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"c",0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M13</b><br />Some masculine polysyllabic nouns with consonant endings whose base form is expanded by -ov- in plural. (<i>galeb, golub</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"ova";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"ove";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ovima";<br /><br /><b>M14</b><br />masculine nouns whose base form ends in "bak". "b" is replaced by "p", "a" is deleted, and appropriate case endings are added. (<i>prisobak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"p",0>"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"p",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"p",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"p",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"p",0>"kom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"p",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"p",0>"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"p",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M15</b><br />Inanimate masculine nouns whose base form ends in a vowel. (<i>defile, rezime, argo, intervju</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M16</b><br />Inanimate masculine nouns whose base form ends in "i". "j" is added between "i" and case endings. (<i>hobi, lobi</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"ja";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"ju";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"ju";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"jem";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"ji";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"ja";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"jima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"je";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"ji";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"jima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"jima";<br /><br /><b>M17</b><br />Inanimate masculine nouns of foreign origin whose base form ends in "o". (<i>kimono, dinamo, konto, loto, duo, korzo, torzo</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br />
 SNG&GNT:=1>"a";<br />
 SNG&DAT:=1>"u";<br />
 SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br />
 SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br />
 SNG&LOC:=1>"u";<br />
 SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br />
 PLR&NOM:=1>"a";<br />
 PLR&GNT:=1>"a";<br />
 PLR&DAT:=1>"ima";<br />
 PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br />
 PLR&VOC:=1>"i";<br />
 PLR&LOC:=1>"ima";<br />
 PLR&INS:=1>"ima";<br />
;<br /><br /><b>M18</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base forms ends in -ac-. "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>starac, klinac, neznanac, stranac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"ca";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"cu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=2>"ca";<br /> SNG&VOC:=2>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"cu";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"cem";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"ce";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M19</b><br />Nouns whose base form ends in -ak-. "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>odsječak, prstenak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"ku";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"kom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M20</b><br />Nouns whose base form ends in -alj-. "a" is deleted in al forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>pedalj</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"lja";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"lju";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"lju";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"lju";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"ljem";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"lji";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"ljima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"lje";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"lji";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"ljima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"ljima";<br /><br /><b>M21</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -am-. "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>obujam</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"ma";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"mu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=2>"me";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"mu";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"mom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"mi";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"mima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"me";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"mi";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"mima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"mima";<br /><br /><b>M22</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -ar-. "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>metar, hektar</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"ra";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"ru";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=2>"re";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"ru";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"rom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"ri";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"rima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"re";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"ri";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"rima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"rima";<br /><br /><b>M23</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -at-. "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>nokat, lakat</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"ta";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"tu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=2>"tu";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"tu";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"tom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"ti";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"tima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"te";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"ti";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"tima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"tima";<br /><br /><b>M24</b><br />Masculine noun "pas" is inflected the same way as nouns whose base form ends in -ac-, -ak-, -alj-,-am-,-ar and -at-. "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive.  (<i>pas</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"sa";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"su";<br /> SNG&ACC:=2>"sa";<br /> SNG&VOC:=2>"se";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"su";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"som";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"si";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"sima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"se";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"si";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"sima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"sima";<br /><br /><b>M25</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -dak-. "d" is replaced by "t" and "a" is deleted in all forms except singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>pomladak, uradak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"t",0>"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"t",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"t",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"t",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"t",0>"kom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"t",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"t",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"t",0>"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"t",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"t",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"t",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M26</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -đak-. "đ" is replaced by "ć" and "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>omeđak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"ć",0>"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"ć",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"ć",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"ć",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"ć",0>"kom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"ć",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"ć",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"ć",0>"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"ć",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"ć",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"ć",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M27</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -zak-. "z" is replaced by "s", and "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>izlazak, odlazak, zalazak, polazak, dolazak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"s",0>"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"s",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"s",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"s",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"s",0>"kom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"s",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"s",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"s",0>"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"s",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"s",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"s",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M28</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -žak-. "ž" is replaced by "š", and "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive. (<i>umnožak</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"š",0>"ka";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"š",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"š",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"š",0>"ku";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"š",0>"kom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"š",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"š",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"š",0>"ke";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"š",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"š",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"š",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M29</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -bac-. "b" is replaced with "p", and "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive (<i>vrabac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=3>"p",0>"ca";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"p",0>"cu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=3>"p",0>"ca";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"p",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"p",0>"cu";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"p",0>"com";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"p",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"p",0>"ce";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"p",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"p",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M30</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -žac-. "ž" is replaced with "š", and "a" is deleted in all forms except for singular nominative and plural genitive (<i>tronožac, crvenokožac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=3>"š",0>"ca";<br /> SNG&DAT:=3>"š",0>"cu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=3>"š",0>"ca";<br /> SNG&VOC:=3>"š",0>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=3>"š",0>"cu";<br /> SNG&INS:=3>"š",0>"cem";<br /> PLR&NOM:=3>"š",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&GNT:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=3>"š",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=3>"š",0>"ce";<br /> PLR&VOC:=3>"š",0>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=3>"š",0>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=3>"š",0>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M31</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -ac-. (<i>gimnazijalac, provincijalac, bijelac, ilegalac, strijelac, svilac, dvokrilac</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"ca";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"cu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=2>"ca";<br /> SNG&VOC:=2>"če";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"cu";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"com";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"ci";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"cima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"ce";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"ci";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"cima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"cima";<br /><br /><b>M32</b><br />Masculine nouns of foreign origin that do not have the so-called "fleeting a" in singular nominative, but it appears in plural genitive. (<i>afekt, subjekt, insekt</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:="a"<[-1],0>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M33</b><br />Masculine noun "čovjek" has a different base form in plural ("ljud-"). (<i>čovjek</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"č",0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=6>"ljud",0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=6>"ljud",0>"i";<br /> PLR&DAT:=6>"ljud",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=6>"ljud",0>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=6>"ljud",0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=6>"ljud",0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=6>"ljud",0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M34</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in "o". "o" is replaced by "l", and "a" is deleted. (<i>orao, kabao, pakao, posao, kotao</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=2>"l",0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=2>"l",0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=2>"l",0>"a";<br /> SNG&VOC:=2>"l",0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=2>"l",0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=2>"l",0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=2>"l",0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&GEN:=2>"l",0>"ova";<br /> PLR&DAT:=2>"l",0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=2>"l",0>"ove";<br /> PLR&VOC:=2>"l",0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&LOC:=2>"l",0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&INS:=2>"l",0>"ovima";<br /><br /><b>M35</b><br />Masculine nouns whose base form ends in -io-. "i" is replaced by "ije", "o" is replaced by "l".   (<i>dio, udio, predio, odio, razdio</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"u";<br /> SNG&LOC:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&GEN:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"ova";<br /> PLR&DAT:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&ACC:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"ove";<br /> PLR&VOC:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&LOC:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&INS:="i":"ije","o":"l",0>"ovima";<br /><br /><b>M36</b><br />Most of the masculine one-syllable nouns, whose base form does not end in a palatal consonant, get -ov- in plural. (<i>grad, grab, štab, zglob, snob, sob, grb, dub, klub, gad</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"ova";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"ove";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ovima";<br /><br /><b>M37</b><br />Most of the masculine one-syllable nouns, whose base form ends in a palatal consonant, get -ev-  in plural. (<i>kraj, plač, mač, skeč, meč, smeč, bič, ranč, linč, prč, vrč, puč, sić, nož, muž</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"em";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"evi";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"eva";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"evima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"eve";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"evi";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"evima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"evima";<br /><br /><b>M38</b><br />Masculine nouns that contain some of the yat reflexes. The long yat reflex ("ije") is replaced by short ("je") in plural. (<i>cvijet, lijek, slijed, snijeg, stijeg, smijeh, mijeh, plijen, cijep, bijes, svijet</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:="ije":"je",0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&GEN:="ije":"je",0>"ova";<br /> PLR&DAT:="ije":"je",0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&ACC:="ije":"je",0>"ove";<br /> PLR&VOC:="ije":"je",0>"ovi";<br /> PLR&LOC:="ije":"je",0>"ovima";<br /> PLR&INS:="ije":"je",0>"ovima";<br /><br /><b>M39</b><br />Masculine nouns that end in "a" in singular nominative. (<i>gazda, vođa, djedica, kalfa, vučina</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M40</b><br />Feminine nouns whose base form does not end in palatal or velar consonant. (<i>škola, mama, žena, čarapa, karta</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M41</b><br />Feminine nouns that end in "ica" form singular vocative with "e" rather than "o". (<i>učiteljica, prijateljica, profesorica</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M42</b><br />Feminine nouns whose base form ends in a velar consonant "k". "k" is replaced by "c" in singular dative and locative. (<i>dlaka, rijeka, muka</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="k":"c",1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:="k":"c",1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M43</b><br />Feminine nouns whose base form ends in a velar "g". "g" is replaced by "z" in singular dative and locative. (<i>sloga, vlaga</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="g":"z",1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:="g":"z",1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M44</b><br />Feminine nouns whose base form ends in a velar consonant "h". "h" is replaced by "s" in singular dative and locative. (<i>utjeha, ovrha</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:="h":"s",1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:="h":"s",1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M45</b><br />There are some feminine nouns whose base form ends in a velar consonant "k", but "k" is not replaced by "c". (<i>štuka, vladika, kika, rika, sika, tuka, Riječanka, Slavonka, Hercegovka</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M46</b><br />There are some feminine nouns whose base form ends in a velar consonant "g", but "g" is not replaced by "z". (<i>kaciga, špaga, raga, saga, liga, figa, felga, sfinga, joga, droga, toga, duga, fuga</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M47</b><br />There are some feminine nouns whose base form ends in a velar consonant "h", but "h" is not replaced by "s". (<i>psiha, sinegdoha, protuha</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M48</b><br />Feminine nouns whose base form ends in "0" (kob-0) or "ost" (rad-ost). "i" is added everywhere except for singular nominative and accusative. "ima" is added dativee, locative and instrumenal. (<i>radost, žalost, mladost, milost, svjetlost, dob, kob, skrb, riječ, žuć, peć, moć, hrid, ćud, žeđ, bol, pogibelj, obitelj, neman, zelen, jesen, kap, večer, zvijer, uš, golijet, vrlet, klijet, pamet, bit, dobit, nit, strast, pošast, pričest, vijest, svijest, kost, bojazan, srž</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M49</b><br />Feminine nouns "kći" has a special kind of paradigm. "er" is added everywhere except for singular nominative. (<i>kći</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> SNG&DAT:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=[2]>"er",1>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> SNG&LOC:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> PLR&NOM:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> PLR&DAT:=[2]>"er",1>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> PLR&VOC:=[2]>"er",1>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=[2]>"er",1>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=[2]>"er",1>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M50</b><br />Feminine noun "mati" has a similar paradigm as the noun "kći". "er" is also added, but with different endings. (<i>mati</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=[3]>"er",1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=[3]>"er",1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"er";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:=[3]>"er",1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=[3]>"er",1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=[3]>"er",1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:=[3]>"er",1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=[3]>"er",1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=[3]>"er",1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=[3]>"er",1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=[3]>"er",1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=[3]>"er",1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M51</b><br />Feminine nouns that have the ending "lju" in singular instrumental. (<i>krv, skrb, glad, bol, kap</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"lju";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"i";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M52</b><br />Feminine nouns whose base form ends in "db", "džb", "žb", "vc", "nč", "ck", ck, "čk", "jk", "ljk", "mk", "nk", "pk", "rk", "sk", "šk", "tk", "vk", "gl", "kl", "tl", "blj", "čm", sm", "šm", "žn", "kn", "sn", "šnj", "dr" "žr", "tr", "nt", "rt", "kv" and tv" have the so-called fleeting a in plural genitive. (<i>ženidba, izložba, narudžba, izložba, ovca, naranča, kocka, igla, pjesma, sestra, smokva</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"i";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:="a"<[-2];<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M53</b><br />Neuter nouns whose base form does not end in a palatal consonant.  (<i>selo, brdo, blago, ruho, mlijeko, pismo, nebo, vreteno, sito, crijevo</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"o";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M54</b><br />Neuter nouns whose base form ends in a palatal consonant or  "c and "r". (<i>polje, vijeće, bezvlađe, narječje, groblje, imanje, sjedište, more, srce, sunce, lice</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"a";<br /> SNG&ACC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"em";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M55</b><br />Some neuter nouns have the infix "en" in all forms except for singular nominative, accusative and vocative. (<i>pleme, sjeme, vrijeme</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=0>"na";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"nu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"nu";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"nom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&GEN:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&DAT:=0>"nima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"na";<br /> PLR&LOC:=0>"nima";<br /> PLR&INS:=0>"nima";<br /><br /><b>M56</b><br />Neuter noun "kumče" has the infix "et" in all forms except for singular nominative, accusative and vocative. Plural is formed by adding "ad". (<i>kumče</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GNT:=0>"ta";<br /> SNG&DAT:=0>"tu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:=0>"tu";<br /> SNG&INS:=0>"tom";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"ad";<br /> PLR&GNT:=1>"adi";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"adi";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"ad";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"adi";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"adi";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"adi";<br /><br /><b>M57</b><br />Neuter noun "dijete" becomes a collective noun in plural. (<i>dijete</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:="ije":"je",0>"ta";<br /> SNG&DAT:="ije":"je",0>"tu";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:="ije":"je",0>"tu";<br /> SNG&INS:="ije":"je",0>"tom";<br /> PLR&NOM:="dijet":"djec",1>"e";<br /> PLR&GEN:="dijet":"djec",1>"e";<br /> PLR&DAT:="dijet":"djec",1>"i";<br /> PLR&ACC:="dijet":"djec",1>"u";<br /> PLR&VOC:="dijet":"djec",1>"o";<br /> PLR&LOC:="dijet":"djec",1>"i";<br /> PLR&INS:="dijet":"djec",1>"om";<br /><br /><b>M58</b><br />Some neuter nouns have fleeting a in plural genitive. (<i>sedlo, veslo, staklo, vitlo, žezlo</i>)<br />SNG&NOM:=0>"";<br /> SNG&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> SNG&DAT:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&ACC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&VOC:=0>"";<br /> SNG&LOC:=1>"u";<br /> SNG&INS:=1>"om";<br /> PLR&NOM:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&GEN:=2>"ala";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M59</b><br />Feminine nouns that  appear only in the plural form and do not have a singular variant for referring to a single object. (<i>gaće, gaćice, hlače, novine, nožice, škare</i>)<br />PLR&NOM:=0>"";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&ACC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&VOC:=1>"e";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ama";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ama";<br /><br /><b>M60</b><br />Neuter nouns that appear only in the plural form and do not have a singular variant for referring to a single object. (<i>vrata, leđa, pluća, usta, križa, kola, nosila</i>)<br />PLR&NOM:=0>"";<br /> PLR&GEN:=1>"a";<br /> PLR&DAT:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&ACC:=0>"";<br /> PLR&VOC:=0>"";<br /> PLR&LOC:=1>"ima";<br /> PLR&INS:=1>"ima";<br /><br /><b>M61</b><br />Verbs whose infinitive base form ends in Ø (null morpheme). In present tense, "s" is replaced by "t" (plesti-pletem. (<i>plesti</i>)<br />INF:="ti">"ti";<br /> PRS&1PS:=3>"tem";<br /> PRS&2PS:=3>"teš";<br /> PRS&3PS:=3>"tu";<br /> PRS&1PP:=3>"temo";<br /> PRS&2PP:=3>"tete";<br /> PRS&3PP:=3>"tu";<br /> IMP&2PS:=3>"ti";<br /> IMP&1PP:=3>"timo";<br /> IMP&2PP:=3>"tite";<br /> PTP&ACV&MCL&SNG:=3>"o";<br /> PTP&ACV&FEM&SNG:=3>"la";<br /> PTP&ACV&NEU&SNG:=3>"lo";<br /> PTP&ACV&MCL&PLR:=3>"li";<br /> PTP&ACV&FEM&PLR:=3>"le";<br /> PTP&ACV&NEU&PLR:=3>"la";<br /> PTP&PSV&MCL&SNG:=3>"ten";<br /> PTP&PSV&FEM&SNG:=3>"tena";<br /> PTP&PSV&NEU&SNG:=3>"teno";<br /> PTP&PSV&MCL&PLR:=3>"teni";<br /> PTP&PSV&FEM&PLR:=3>"tene";<br /> PTP&PSV&NEU&PLR:=3>"tena";<br /> PAS&PFV&1PS:=3>"toh";<br /> PAS&PFV&2PS:=3>"te";<br /> PAS&PFV&3PS:=3>"te";<br /> PAS&PFV&1PP:=3>"tosmo";<br /> PAS&PFV&2PP:=3>"toste";<br /> PAS&PFV&3PP:=3>"toše";<br /> PAS&NPFV&1PS:=3>"tijah";<br /> PAS&NPFV&2PS:=3>"tijaše";<br /> PAS&NPFV&3PS:=3>"tijaše";<br /> PAS&NPFV&1PP:=3>"tijasmo";<br /> PAS&NPFV&